From eb74d3a0a9600394978b0392fe13da4d839278a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KC Hema Prasanna <93081094+Hemaprasannakc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:10:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inductor): relayout reshapes that cut the stick dim off a
 boundary

A reshape whose new innermost dim is not a multiple of the stick (W=160 is
2.5 sticks of 64) is not a view on this hardware. The destination pads each
row up to a whole stick, so source and destination are different byte
layouts and the data has to move. PyTorch decides view-vs-copy from host
contiguity, which no longer implies the device layouts match, so the backend
receives a view it cannot honour: splits fail to form a coordinate
("Unsupported coordinate expression 5*c1/2") and merges silently read every
row after the first from the wrong address.

Add a post-grad FX pass that detects these by shape arithmetic and performs
the relayout with primitives the backend already has. A dim the reshape
leaves alone is permuted onto the stick (an on-device restickify), the
split or merge then happens on ordinary non-stick dims where it is free, a
new spyre::rebase_copy materialises the view so the restickify back reads
dense dims rather than a flattened coordinate, and a final permute+clone
restores the layout the original reshape produced. Reshapes with no spare
dim, unsupported dtypes, oversized intermediates, a multi-stick pivot with
nothing non-unit in front of the body, or a cat along the stick dim take
the existing spyre.reshape_via_cpu host path, so no case regresses.

normalize_coordinates additionally only fuses two digits of one variable
when the inner dim is densely packed; fusing across a padded inner dim read
over the gap and produced wrong values.

Measured on a 58-case shape matrix (ranks 1-6, prime widths, sub-stick,
six op spellings, seven consumers, fp16/bf16/fp32/int32/int64): 13 OK /
40 ERR / 5 wrong-value before, 55 OK / 3 ERR / 0 wrong-value after; the
three remaining are eager mode and a non-contiguous input, both out of
scope. The epic's own cases go from 50 OK / 5 wrong-value to 78 OK / 0
wrong-value. test_restickify.py (749) and the coordinate tests pass
unchanged.

The outer-dim merge, when one is needed, is materialised rather than left
as a plain view: Inductor folds free views away, so consumers with a rank
restriction (a depthwise conv) otherwise see the pivot's higher-rank
intermediate.

Fixes #5227
Fixes #5214
Fixes #5224
Fixes #5320
Refs #1353, #5197, #5321, #5872
Supersedes the host-path workaround in #5222

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
